# No-answer queries: nothing in memories.jsonl answers these, so every result the
# ranked path returns for them is a false positive. rel is empty BY CONSTRUCTION —
# that is what marks a query negative, and it is why the graded metrics skip them
# (a query with no relevant item has no defined recall) while the false-positive
# report measures what search returns anyway. This is the baseline the abstention
# work needs: how confident does Ghost look when it has nothing?
#
# Two flavours, both needed. The `off_domain` ones share no vocabulary with the
# corpus, so they measure the floor. The `near_miss` ones reuse corpus vocabulary
# (unit tests, ingress, restore, on-call, disk usage) while asking about
# something the corpus never recorded — those are where a score-based abstain
# rule has to earn its keep, and they are the reason this file exists.
# Vectors are in negative_embeddings.json under each query's name, embedded with
# the query task prefix the production client applies since #642 (EmbedQuery,
# "search_query: ", nomic-embed-text:v1.5 at 768 dims) so they are comparable
# with the graded fixture's query vectors. See docs/benchmarks.md ("No-answer
# queries").
